@table
Banking term | Meaning
**Asset** of a bank | **Loans** (to farmers, industry), investments, cash
**Liability** of a bank | **Deposits** (time deposits are the largest), borrowings from RBI
**NPA** | Loan with interest or principal **overdue for more than 90 days**
**Capital adequacy** (CRAR) | Basel III minimum 8% plus buffers; RBI requires **11.5%**
**DICGC** (1978) | **Wholly owned RBI subsidiary**; insures deposits up to **Rs. 5 lakh** per depositor per bank (since February 2020; Rs. 1 lakh before)
@end

