@section 11.6 | Instruments and Plastic Money

@q 8:96-97

@q 8:151-154

The **Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881** came into force on **1 March 1882**; it covers **cheques, bills of exchange and promissory notes**. India's first **International Financial Services Centre** is **GIFT City** (Gandhinagar, 2015); IFSCA regulates it.

@up UP link: **SIDBI** is headquartered in **Lucknow**. The first RRB, **Prathama Bank**, began in **Moradabad** (UP, 1975). Under "One State, One RRB", UP's RRBs merged into the **Uttar Pradesh Gramin Bank** (2025). **Allahabad Bank** (1865, Prayagraj) and **Awadh Commercial Bank** (Faizabad, 1881) were born in UP.

